{"causes": ["The inherent aristocratic privilege of the Gramont family provided Antoine V with direct access to military and diplomatic appointments within the French court.", "The continuous warfare of Louis XIV's reign created ample opportunities for noblemen like Gramont to gain military experience and advance through the ranks.", "The established system of military and gubernatorial patronage under the French monarchy allowed influential families to secure key positions for their members."], "effects": ["Antoine V de Gramont's military service contributed to the French Crown's strategic objectives during the Nine Years' War and the War of the Spanish Succession.", "His diplomatic mission to Spain helped to reinforce the Bourbon dynastic ties between France and Spain during a critical period of succession.", "His legacy perpetuated the Gramont family's tradition of military command and regional governance in France, influencing subsequent generations of French nobility."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "antoine-v-de-gramont", "sourceName": "Antoine V de Gramont", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "nine-years-war", "targetName": "Nine Years' War", "context": "Antoine V de Gramont participated in major campaigns of the Nine Years' War, including the Battle of Steenkirk in 1692."}, {"sourceSlug": "louis-xiv", "sourceName": "Louis XIV", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "antoine-v-de-gramont", "targetName": "Antoine V de Gramont", "context": "Louis XIV's extensive military campaigns provided the primary context and opportunity for Antoine V de Gramont's military career and advancement."}, {"sourceSlug": "antoine-v-de-gramont", "sourceName": "Antoine V de Gramont", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "france", "targetName": "France", "context": "Antoine V de Gramont served as Governor of Navarre and Béarn, positions of regional power within the Kingdom of France."}, {"sourceSlug": "antoine-v-de-gramont", "sourceName": "Antoine V de Gramont", "verb": "COLLAB